{
 "source": "NIST CFReDS Data Leakage Case, answer key dated 2018-07-23: https://cfreds-archive.nist.gov/data_leakage_case/leakage-answers.pdf",
 "what_this_is": "The ground truth we score against. One item per answer row of the questions about the leak itself. Each item says which evidence row should exist: kind, entity and time.",
 "selection_rule": "Questions 16, 21, 22, 26, 28, 33, 35, 36, 51 and 55 of section 6: searches, e-mails, devices, opened files, CD burning, the resignation letter, deleted files and files copied to RM#2. Every answer row of those questions is included, whether or not the pipeline can produce it. The list was fixed before the first scored run.",
 "not_included_yet": "Questions about system configuration, installed applications, cloud storage, shell bags, thumbnails, Windows Search and shadow copies. Mapping to the 20 items Mulder scores is open (TASKS.md, lane 4).",
 "time_zone": "NIST prints Eastern Daylight Time (UTC-4 on these dates). 'utc' is that time converted; 'nist_local_time' is the value as printed.",
 "tolerance_s": 2,
